<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Grupo Carso lowered.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Grupo Carso lowered.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- JP Morgan downgraded Mexican conglomerate Grupo Carso to long-term buy from buy.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Mary Bourque said the move was based mostly on the rich valuation of the shares. &quot;We also consider in this recommendation the lack of major strategic moves we forsee the company making at this time,&quot; she wrote.</p>
<p>-- She raised her 1996 and 1997 earnings estimate for the company, mostly due to non-cash items, to 3.36 pesos and 3.29 pesos, from 3.05 and 3.17 pesos, respectively.</p>
<p>-- Carso was up 10 centavos to 48.10 pesos in early trade on Tuesday.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom, +525 728-9565))</p>
</text>
